    measured_ramp_capability: { cell: "U", ev: "STILL UNTESTED and DELIBERATELY NOT MINTED at miso-156 — that session measured FLEET ramp, not the PER-ASSET reserve qualifier, so no verdict is taken. Two committed MISO measurements now stand against it and a successor must confront both: (a) MISO's model UNDER-ramps its own measured fleet at every quantile of every year (miso-156 §7.2, |1-h move| ratio 0.83/0.83/0.88 at p99), and (b) miso-153's D-4 found reserves INERT at the summer peak — ZERO binding hours, zero shortfall, dual $0.00, across all three families x three years x 1,464 Jun+Jul hours. A qualifier that tightens a constraint which never binds cannot move a price. Rule 28(d): NYISO's I does not transfer. miso-204 (2026-09-03, NO LP) ADDS A CAUTION TO ANY SUCCESSOR AND MINTS NOTHING (cell stays U): the 'evening ramp' framing this queue item inherited from miso-203 was measured on the RAW EST hour-ending index, while the model and the C3a scoring reference are on fixed CST with Feb 29 dropped (a pure -1 h shift, r = 1.000000 at k = -1 in 2023/2025; -1 h then -25 h across leap-day 2024). On the corrected instrument miso-203's '13 of 15 in h18-h21' becomes 4 of 15, the concentration is 11 of 15 in h15-h18 CST, and the mean hour-of-day migration is one large step then flat (11.67 -> 15.73 -> 15.87), not the three-year march reported. A ramp product's phase 0 must therefore RE-ESTABLISH its window on the corrected instrument before any field is minted, and must still confront the two standing measurements against it (miso-156 §7.2 the model UNDER-ramps its own fleet at every quantile; miso-153's D-4 reserves INERT at the summer peak). Record FINDING-miso204-the-tail-is-energy-and-the-comparator-is-one-hub-2026-09-03.md. miso-205 (2026-09-03, NO LP, CELL STAYS U, NOTHING MINTED) DISCHARGES miso-204's re-establish-the-window precondition AND ADDS A THIRD OBJECTION THIS FAMILY MUST NOW CLEAR. The window is re-established on the repaired instrument (N-1 reproduces miso-204's object set exactly; N-2 reproduces miso-203's own comparison row exactly): the object is a LATE-AFTERNOON set, mean hour-of-day 15.87 CST in 2025 over seven distinct days, and its 3-h net-load ramp is 4,930 MW against a Jun-Jul mean of 26 - large in absolute terms. BUT THE RAMP DOES NOT DISCRIMINATE: the ordinary top-15 GROSS-LOAD Jun-Jul hours carry a LARGER 3-h ramp, 5,364 MW, so a ramp-keyed product would hit the ordinary summer peak hours at least as hard as the object's, and ramp does not separate the two populations. The inherited 'evening ramp after solar roll-off' framing is refuted outright on both halves - 'evening' by miso-204 (4 of 15 in h18-h21, not 13) and 'after solar roll-off' by miso-205 (solar 6,237 MW, +34% ABOVE the Jun-Jul mean, contribution to the net-load elevation -6.7% rather than the +11.5% reported; hour-of-day-matched solar p48.1, i.e. ordinary). The renewable anomaly is WIND (h-o-d matched p36.5) and even that carries only +11.9% of the elevation against load's 94.8%. A phase 0 must therefore clear THREE objections, not two: this non-discrimination result, miso-156 s7.2 (the model UNDER-ramps its own measured fleet at every quantile of every year, ratio 0.83/0.83/0.88 at p99) and miso-153's D-4 (reserves INERT at the summer peak) - on top of the still-unanswered PRIMARY-SOURCE question of whether MISO's real market prices a ramp product in these hours at all. Rule 28(d): NYISO's I still does not transfer. Record FINDING-miso205-the-object-is-load-and-wind-not-solar-2026-09-03.md." },
