    unit_outage_per_unit_clip: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-202 (2026-09-03) — **KEEPER 2026-09-03-miso-202-unitclip**, ALL TEN A/B GATES PASSING. Row added WITH the field the same day (rule 28c) and adjudicated in the same session. THE IDENTIFICATION, published before the mechanism existed (_miso202_boundary_day_phase0.json committed BEFORE the PREREG and before a line of mechanism code): outages.unit_outage_event_window reconstructs a day-granular extract row as [outage_start, outage_end + 1 day), so two windows of the SAME unit sharing a boundary date BOTH cover that day while _unit_outage_factors_from_events SUMS row shares rather than unioning them — the unit's capacity is subtracted TWICE for 24 h on a day it can be at most 100 % out. WHAT SETTLES IT AS A DEFECT RATHER THAN A JUDGEMENT CALL IS THE CENSUS'S SHAPE, NOT ITS SIZE: every one of the 845 same-unit window overlaps is EXACTLY 24.0 h (std5d 648, lay-up 197, short 0) — a single-bin histogram, the fingerprint of the '+ 1 day' artifact and of nothing else. N-1 reproduction PASS on 589 bins across all three layers that share the accumulator. IT IS WIDER THAN THE INSTRUMENT THAT FOUND IT COULD SEE: miso-201 met the object only where it OVERFLOWED a steam bin and sized it at '24-72 h/yr per bin'; measured class-agnostically it is 845 pairs over 63 bins restoring 91.1/77.6/103.4 GWh across CC_REGULAR (55.9/17.3/50.2), ST_GAS (32.0/56.3/50.6), COAL, CC_CHP and ST_CHP — and an overflowing cell is precisely where it is INERT (the correct answer there is 0.0 and the clip already delivers it), which is why an overflow-scoped census could not see the live part. THE REPAIR IS A CEILING ON A SUM, not a window-merging heuristic: no date arithmetic, no adjacency test, no tolerance, ZERO free parameters (rule 21), so it is the identity except in the physically impossible case and can only ever remove LESS. The ceiling is the LARGEST capacity a unit's own rows claim, so a mid-extract re-rating cannot clip a legitimate single window; it clips PER UNIT not per bin, so two DIFFERENT units out concurrently still zero the bin. SCOPE BY MEASUREMENT: std >=5-day + short + partial + LAY-UP together (rule 19 — their shares are contractually additive), MAXGEN EXCLUDED because phase-0 N-5 measured ZERO same-unit overlaps over 544 unit-series (its windows are already hour-granular, so it cannot carry a boundary-DAY defect); a signature assertion in the tests fails if a future edit wires it in. THE A/B: S-0 BIT-IDENTICAL (9 sidecars, max_abs_diff 0.0 — also the end-to-end proof of byte-inertness while off), S-1 exactly one field, S-2 std5d 31 / lay-up 12 gaining and short 0 (a falsifiable phase-0 prediction confirmed against production), S-3 MONOTONICITY — a HARD VOID this lever earns — PASS on 589 bins with ZERO bin-hours removing more and worst regression exactly 0.000e+00, K-1 NO BAND EXIT ANYWHERE, K-2/K-3/K-4/K-5 silent (zero new D-4 off-window binding, zero D-1 flips, zero PASS->non-PASS, status map IDENTICAL), K-6 REAL (D1=30/D2=23/D4=57 on BOTH legs, diagnostics and attestations generated for both legs BEFORE scoring — the miso-200 vacuous-pass trap closed in advance). Determination UNCHANGED at NOT-YET on price_mean with C3c the single ledgered caveat. REPORTED AGAINST THE PROMOTION: the named risk CC_REGULAR-2024 +6.931 -> +6.942 moved adversely as pre-registered (1.069 TWh headroom); the arm is SMALL in dispatch (largest C1 move +0.026 TWh) and is justified as a DEFECT REPAIR, never as a residual improvement; C3a 2023/2025 UNCHANGED and 2024 -4.5820 -> -4.6130, reported and NEVER the justification (rule 1); C8 deltas below the 0.0005 inertness epsilon. audit_keepers --iso MISO PASS 0/0." },
