    ct_peaker_committed_measured: { cell: ".", ev: "n/a AS A CAISO-GATED FIELD — but MISO IS THIS REPAIR'S PRECEDENT, and that is why the cell carries evidence rather than a bare dot (caiso-241, 2026-09-03, config-only census, zero solves). MISO's CT_PEAKER committed is ALREADY 1.025 = its own phys_committed 1.025 to the third decimal — the only one of the six ISOs whose CT min-load band is grounded on its own measured avg_committed_p50 — and _MISO_OFFER_CURVE states the caiso-241 rule-19 argument verbatim: \"The commitment-cost component of the real MISO CT offer (start + no-load recovery) is NOT a static heat-rate multiplier: MISO's ELMP (FERC Order 825 fast-start pricing) folds fast-start startup/no-load offer costs into the LMP, represented by the P1 startup amortization on the CT econ/peak tranches ... not by a band multiplier here.\" Nothing is asked of this lane and no value transfers in either direction (rule 25). results/calibration/PRECOMMIT-caiso241-ct-peaker-committed-2026-09-03.md §1 (the five-limb admissibility ruling) + PRECOMMIT-caiso241-ADDENDUM-arm-2026-09-03.md §A2-§A6 (G-STRUCT pre-solve, the fuel-invariant decomposition, the two-sided §H' envelope), results/calibration/_caiso241_gstruct_presolve.json, _caiso241_cell_bound.json." },
    nyiso_ct_peaker_bands_measured: { cell: "U", ev: "row added at nyiso-199 (2026-09-06) with the NYISO-gated field (rule 28c). UNTESTED here and NO NYISO VERDICT TRANSFERS (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]): the field raises a hard ValueError on any non-NYISO ISO. This ISO may carry the SAME defect in kind — five of six ISO CT_PEAKER curves price the min-load band above their own measured avg_committed_p50 (ERCOT 1.480/1.022, CAISO 1.350/0.991, PJM 1.250/1.049, NYISO 1.350/0.843, NEISO 1.350/0.985; MISO is the one that grounded it at 1.025/1.025) — but arming it here needs this lane's OWN zero-LP census: whether the class's deficit is INTERIOR rather than availability- or floor-bound, whether tranche_startup_amortization is armed on this ISO's keeper (the rule 19 double-count leg), and this ISO's own phys_* keys." },
