    gas_offer_curve_tranches: { cell: "K", ev: "miso-152 (2026-08-11) KEEPS cell K -- the mechanism is NOT refuted -- and records a MEASURED FILL-ORDER caveat on it, closing the base-band inversion thread miso-151 section 8 named but did not open (charter B, Phase 0, NO solve, NO run registered). WHY THE BANDS INVERT: deliberately. _MISO_OFFER_CURVE grounds the committed band in the measured CAMPD part-load premium and the source comment records the PREVIOUS state (committed 0.92 < econ_low 0.95) as the defect it was fixing, so the inversion is not itself a bug. WHAT IT OPENS IS: the LP fills tranches in COST order while physics fills them in OUTPUT-POSITION order; there is NO same-plant fill-order constraint anywhere in the LP (lp/bounds.py sets col_lower = min_gen else pmin per independent column; the only group row in lp/rows.py is the hydro envelope), and MISO floors NOTHING on the CC committed tranche (pmin AND min_gen are 0.0 on all 44 CC_REGULAR committed rows, all 8760 h). So a CC plant produces its incremental bands while its 515.97 MW min-load block sits idle -- real plant p991: committed 515.97 MW @ $26.184 with econc00-02 at 36.85 MW each @ $25.122/$25.643/$26.164, all three CHEAPER than the block they physically sit on. CONFIRMED AT THREE LEVELS: source (G-1), effective mc through the real offer path (G-2: committed dearer than an econ sub in 1,167,048 of 2,312,640 plant-band-hours = 50.5 %, mean gap $0.833/MWh, ~3 of the 6 smoothed subs per plant), and a live solve_dispatch (G-3, 4/4 tests, tests/test_miso152_fillorder.py). AND IT IS IMMATERIAL: out-of-order energy is 0.36/0.31/0.45 % of CC energy (2023/24/25) against a pre-registered prior of 25 % band [5,60] -- REFUTED ~55x, below the band floor -- because the object is WIDE BUT THIN (each econ sub is 7 % of the min-load block and the price window is ~$1/MWh wide), touching 39-43 of 44 plants in 7,118/7,200/10,693 plant-hours. T-6 (reconstruction vs committed class_hourly) PASSES on CC: -1.83/-1.01/+9.42 %. NO LEVER PROPOSED: the sign is REPAIR-DEPENDENT and both limbs are small -- R-a PIN (min-load must-take whenever the plant runs, the ERCOT-141 floor_online_hours mechanism) gives +1.06/+0.87/+1.49 % CC supply, price DOWN, WRONG way for the -15.6 % miss; R-b GATE (no upper band unless the min-load block clears) gives -0.36/-0.31/-0.45 %, price UP and tiny. PREREG P-2 was registered with a band spanning zero and section 7 disclosed the author's prior expectation of UP before measuring; picking a limb to get a sign would be fitting the repair to the residual (rule 1 second half). NAMED SUCCESSOR, NOT OPENED: CT_PEAKER carries the SAME inversion with the largest gap in the fleet ($12.50-25.89/MWh, 15-30x CC's) and its 79 committed rows are as UNFLOORED as CC's, but its T-6 FAILS (+38.8/+37.9/+40.1 %; ST_GAS -38.0/-39.2/-59.3 %) so its reconstructed 1.20/0.54/6.47 % out-of-order share is DESCRIPTIVE ONLY and no verdict rests on it -- measuring it needs an instrument that reproduces CT commitment. Keeper 2026-08-09-miso-148-basis-aware UNCHANGED, fail set still {C3a, C3b}. FINDING-miso152-the-inversion-is-real-and-immaterial-2026-08-11.md; PREREG-miso152-tranche-fill-order-2026-08-11.md." },
