    entry_pipeline_aware_signal: { cell: "O", fc: "O", ev: "FFR-5C (docs/handoffs/ffr-5c-entry-cap-fix-2026-08-05.md; paired arm scripts/probes/ffr5c_paired_arm.py, regression tests tests/unit/model/test_entry_pipeline_aware_signal.py). PAIRED ARM ON BOTH FFR-4A SIGNATURES, arm selected by the shipped field rather than by editing source, so it reproduces from a clean checkout. MISO SOLAR (ladder-first cell, EIA-860 vintage_2020 seed 0.618 GW): shipped 1,236 MW/yr FROZEN forever (2.472 GW commissioned 2021-25, 14.832 GW decided 2022-33); armed 1,236 -> 2,472 -> 4,944 -> 6,000 -> 6,000, i.e. the ratchet doubles as ReEDS specifies until the 6,000 MW/yr static per-tech cap becomes the TRUE binder (3.708 GW commissioned, 62.652 GW decided). MISO WIND (static-cap-first cell, seed 4.367 GW ⇒ ladder 8,734 MW/yr, never the binder): shipped alternates 4,000 / 0 / 4,000 / 0 with mean 2,000 MW = C/L exactly - the general law measured directly; armed 4,000 MW/yr flat = C, alternation killed. Every leg matches FFR-4A §5.2's measured Arm 0 and Arm B to the MW with ZERO deviation, so no finding needed explaining. BYTE-IDENTITY PROVEN, not asserted: cache_key(ScenarioConfig()) is unchanged at 603c2498bf71d21d (field registered in _CACHE_KEY_OPTIONAL_FIELDS + the default ledger), the two shipped-arm series above are asserted as regression tests, and _lookahead_reprice_signal with the three new parameters at their None defaults reproduces the pre-FFR-5C array under assert_array_equal." },
